tion.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ideal}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\operatorname{Ideal}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"6e4f95381faac4f9\" href=\"?note=6e4f95381faac4f9\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-ideal.md\">../batch05/58-df-ideal.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcIdeal7IdealProjection}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcIdeal7IdealProjection}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}ideal7\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}projection} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcIdeal7IdealProjection}_S(X,\\mathcal I,Y,\\mathcal J,f)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Ideal}(\\mathcal I,\\mathcal P(X))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,Y)\\land\\mathcal J=\\left\\{B\\subseteq Y:\\{x\\in X:f(x)\\in B\\}\\in\\mathcal I\\right\\}\\land\\operatorname{Ideal}(\\mathcal J,\\mathcal P(Y))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}ideal7\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}projection} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcIdeal7IdealProjection}_S(X,\\mathcal I,Y,\\mathcal J,f)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Ideal}(\\mathcal I,\\mathcal P(X))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(f,X,Y)\\land\\mathcal J=\\left\\{B\\subseteq Y:\\{x\\in X:f(x)\\in B\\}\\in\\mathcal I\\right\\}\\land\\operatorname{Ideal}(\\mathcal J,\\mathcal P(Y))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The upstream ideal predicate ranges over a family of subsets, so its second argument is the relevant powerset. The inverse image is expanded as an explicit subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span>, avoiding an undeclared inverse-image operator.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"